---Optional matching criteria. If omitted entirely, the rule acts as match-all. All non-empty
---fields in this block must match (logical AND).
---@class stackit.vpn.UpdateGatewayBGPFilterRuleRequestMatch
---@field asPathContainsAny? stackit.vpn.UpdateGatewayBGPFilterRuleRequestMatchAsPathContainsAnyList Matches if the AS-PATH contains any one of the listed ASNs (logical OR within the list). Treated as an unordered set; ordering is not preserved by the storage layer. When combined with firstASN, both conditions must hold (logical AND, consistent with the rest of the match block). If firstASN is also listed here, its presence as the first hop is sufficient to satisfy this list; no duplicate hop is required.
---@field communities? stackit.vpn.UpdateGatewayBGPFilterRuleRequestMatchCommunitiesList Matches if the route carries any one of these BGP standard communities (logical OR within the list). Format is 'asn:value' per RFC 1997 (both halves must fit in a uint32, i.e. 0..4294967295). Extended, large and well-known communities are not supported.
---@field firstASN? number Matches if the first ASN (immediate neighbor) in the AS-PATH equals this ASN. Combines with asPathContainsAny using logical AND: when both are set, the first ASN must equal firstASN AND the path must additionally contain at least one ASN from asPathContainsAny.
---@field maxPrefixLength? number Maximum subnet mask length for matched prefixes. May be set together with 'prefixes' (narrows matches to subnets at most this long) or alone (matches any IPv4 route with a mask length <= this value, equivalent to implicit 'prefixes: [0.0.0.0/0]').
---@field minPrefixLength? number Minimum subnet mask length for matched prefixes. May be set together with 'prefixes' (narrows matches to subnets at least this long) or alone (matches any IPv4 route with a mask length >= this value, equivalent to implicit 'prefixes: [0.0.0.0/0]'). If both minPrefixLength and maxPrefixLength are set, minPrefixLength must be <= maxPrefixLength.
---@field peer? string Matches the exact IPv4 address of the BGP neighbor that advertised the route. Useful when the same filter is attached to multiple tunnels with different neighbor IPs (allows per-peer rules in a shared filter). When a filter is attached to a single tunnel, this field is effectively a no-op because the route-map is already neighbor-scoped.
---@field prefixes? stackit.vpn.UpdateGatewayBGPFilterRuleRequestMatchPrefixesList List of IPv4 networks to match. A route's prefix matches if it equals one of these (subject to minPrefixLength/maxPrefixLength refinement). If omitted, an implicit 0.0.0.0/0 base is used when minPrefixLength or maxPrefixLength is set; if all three are omitted, prefix matching is not performed at all. Each entry must parse as a valid IPv4 CIDR; the network portion is normalised (10.0.0.5/24 → 10.0.0.0/24).

